+# Contract: Plugin Marketplace
+
+## Registry (`src/registry/index.ts`) — `createRegistry(): RegistryService`
+- [ ] register stores plugin manifest → test: registry.test.ts "register stores plugin manifest"
+- [ ] get retrieves registered plugin (latest? — get('name') with no version returns *a* stored version) → test: "get retrieves registered plugin"
+- [ ] get returns null for unregistered → test
+- [ ] list returns all plugins (all versions) → test
+- [ ] search finds by name substring → test
+- [ ] search finds by description substring → test
+- [ ] remove deletes plugin version, returns true → test
+- [ ] listVersions returns all versions for a plugin → test
+- [ ] getVersion(name, version) returns specific version or null → integration test
+- [ ] update(name, version, updates) partial update → interface requirement (no direct unit test but must implement)
+- In-memory SQLite (better-sqlite3, `:memory:`) since createRegistry() is called fresh per test with no shared file path.
+
+## Resolver (`src/resolver/index.ts`) — `createResolver(): ResolverService`
+- [ ] satisfies(version, range) uses semver.satisfies → test
+- [ ] resolve(constraints, available) returns ResolvedVersion[] using maxSatisfying per constraint, preserving constraint order → test
+- [ ] resolve throws for unsatisfiable constraint → test
+- [ ] maxSatisfying(versions, range) → test
+- [ ] validRange(range) → true/false, no throw → test
+- [ ] resolve handles multiple independent constraints with same name (two entries for 'shared-lib') → integration test expects both resolved independently, in order
+
+## Runner (`src/runner/index.ts`) — `createRunner(): RunnerService`
+- [ ] execute(code, context?) wraps code in function body ("return X;"), runs in vm, returns {success, output, duration, memoryUsed}
+- [ ] execute provides context variables accessible in code → test
+- [ ] execute captures object output via toEqual → test
+- [ ] execute reports duration >= 0 → test
+- [ ] execute catches runtime errors → success false, error contains message → test
+- [ ] execute isolates between runs (no shared global state / no `var` leakage) → new vm.createContext() per execute call
+- [ ] executeWithTimeout(code, timeoutMs, context?) kills long-running code (infinite loop) within timeout, success false, error defined, duration > 0 → test
+- Use Node vm module (vm.Script + vm.createContext, script.runInContext with timeout option)
+
+## Reviews (`src/reviews/index.ts`) — `createReviewSystem(): ReviewService`
+- [ ] addReview creates review with auto id (>0), flagged=false, createdAt defined → test
+- [ ] getReviews(pluginName) returns all reviews (all versions) for that plugin name → test + integration "review aggregation across versions"
+- [ ] getAverageRating(pluginName) excludes flagged reviews, average of ratings, returns 0 if none → test
+- [ ] flagReview(id) sets flagged true → test
+- [ ] getFlaggedReviews() returns only flagged → test
+- [ ] removeReview(id) returns true, deletes → test
+- [ ] getReviewsByUser(userId) → test
+- [ ] getReviewCount(pluginName) counts all versions → test
+- In-memory SQLite
+
+## Deps (`src/deps/index.ts`) — `createDepsService(): DepsService`
+- [ ] buildTree(name, registry) recursive DependencyNode tree using latest/any version manifest's dependencies → test
+- [ ] detectCycles(name, registry) DFS cycle detection, returns array of cycles (each a string[] path) or null → test
+- [ ] topologicalSort(name, registry) returns deps-first order ending with root name → test (diamond case: dedup nodes, length 4)
+- [ ] flattenDependencies(name, registry) returns all transitive deps (unique), excludes root → test
+- [ ] hasCircularDependency(name, registry) boolean → test
+
+## Integration (`src/index.ts`) — `createMarketplace(): Marketplace`
+- [ ] Marketplace type exported with registry, resolver, runner, reviews, deps, installPlugin
+- [ ] installPlugin validates manifest: name, version, entryPoint required (non-empty) → throws /Invalid/ on missing
+- [ ] installPlugin registers the plugin in registry
+- [ ] installPlugin resolves dependency versions against registry.listVersions for each dep
+- [ ] installPlugin checks circular deps via deps.hasCircularDependency → throws /Circular/ if found
+- [ ] installPlugin executes entryPoint via runner.execute, returns { resolved, sandboxResult }
+- [ ] plugin with no dependencies → resolved = [], sandbox success
+- [ ] types.ts SHA-256 checksum must remain a689d3f8ff186f56d180f66bb33b394e118b0721e7b8685b307b03991bbf9751 (DO NOT EDIT)
+
+## Build/Lint
+- [ ] npm run build (tsc) succeeds with no errors
+- [ ] npm run lint (eslint) passes with no errors
+- [ ] npm test — all 55 tests pass
